4. Files changed
------------------------------------------------------------------------
- supabase/schema_phase84_safe_cross_party_profile_access.sql (NEW)
    - Drops profiles_select_via_shared_request and
      profiles_select_via_shared_conversation entirely.
      profiles_select_own_or_admin is untouched.
    - Creates public.business_contact_public — a view exposing only
      (id, full_name, company_name), owned by postgres (same
      security_invoker = false / SQL-editor-ownership technique as
      publishers_public in schema_phase82), with its own WHERE clause
      that's a direct column-restricted translation of the two dropped
      policies' exists() checks, plus an own-row branch (so a business
      viewing themselves through this view, e.g. their own entry in
      their own Messages.tsx conversation list, still resolves) and an
      admin branch for completeness.
    - Grants SELECT on the view to authenticated (not anon — no
      legitimate logged-out use case for this).

- src/lib/businessContact.ts (NEW)
    - fetchBusinessContacts(businessIds): batches a lookup against
      business_contact_public for a set of business ids and returns a
      Map for client-side merging. This is a separate top-level query,
      not a PostgREST embed, deliberately: embedding resolves through a
      real foreign-key constraint, and business_contact_public has no FK
      from requests/conversations pointing at it (only the base profiles
      table does) — relying on a view being embeddable under a different
      name isn't something to bet a security fix on across PostgREST
      versions without being able to test it live.

